list_sessions — evaluation
===========================

status: planned (2026-07-09)
focal tool: list_sessions (plans/list_sessions)

task
----
answer availability questions about the installed library — what
session images exist, what could be built — before committing to a
loading strategy.

setup
-----
fresh server (the D1 structure gives ~134 sessions; HOL heap
present, most others not — per the bundled distribution).

prompt
------
"Before we start: I plan to formalize some results that need
multiset reasoning and possibly probability theory. Survey what
this Isabelle installation offers for that — which relevant
sessions exist, and which of them are ready to use right now
versus would need building first."

success
-------
relevant sessions named from tool output (HOL-Library for
multisets, HOL-Probability), each tagged correctly as heap-present
or needing a build (heap_present field).

signals
-------
- pattern use: does the agent query with patterns ("HOL-*",
  "*Prob*") or pull everything and read? both fine; a non-matching
  pattern must read as "no match", not an error (plans/
  list_sessions pinned probe-safety — this eval exercises it
  naturally when the agent probes "Multiset*" which matches no
  SESSION, being a theory name).
- the session/theory confusion: multisets are a THEORY in
  HOL-Library, not a session. does the agent recover from the
  category mismatch and pivot to list_theories/search_sources?
  (this is the discovery-chain handoff working or not.)
- heap_present comprehension: is "ready vs needs building"
  answered from the field, or guessed?

reflection
----------
- if the session/theory category error strands agents, the
  descriptions of the three discovery tools must form an explicit
  chain ("sessions contain theories; for theories see
  list_theories") — write it as a paragraph shared across them.
